\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Central Bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to supports the real-traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 19:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday to lift the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from two-year lows, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real strengthened quickly to 2.075 per dollar in mid-afternoon after earlier to falling to an intraday low of 2.104 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Nervousness about the U.S. economic slowdown and expectations of an imminent economic policy announcement from neighboring Argentina dragged the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its second lowest ever close on Wednesday since it was introduced in mid-1994. \par \par \uc2  The real on Wednesday ended the session at 2.078 per dollar, the lowest close since it ended at 2.17 per dollar on March 2, 1999, a couple of months after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was devalued amid an emerging markets crisis. \par \par \uc2  Brazilian market players anxiously awaited news from Argentina, where developments have added to uncertainty in the market. Newly appointed Argentine Economy Minister Ricardo Lopez Murphy is due to announce measures on Friday to get the neighboring economy out of 2-1/2 years of stagnation. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3f04012\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
