\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real ends at 2-year low despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nicholas Winning \par \uc2 623 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 00:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real closed at its second-lowest-ever level on Thursday after \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide on the back of U.S. and Argentine economic jitters, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real fell to 2.097 per dollar from 2.078 per dollar on Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was born in mid-1994, has closed weaker just once before when it ended at 2.17 per dollar on March 2, 1999, a couple of months after its devaluation. \par \par \uc2  After the close, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monetary Policy Director Luiz Fernando Figueiredo said the Bank had sold three lots of dollars. He justified the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying the real had stopped reflecting the economy, but denied the Bank was dictating to the market. \par \par \uc2  "We have no intention of defining the price, floor or ceiling, because it is a floating exchange rate," he said. "The market took on a life of its own, dislocating itself from the fundamentals of the Brazilian economy." \par \par \uc2  Figueiredo did say that the foreign markets were turbulent, but declined to give the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or whether he thought the real was now under control. \par \par \uc2  "We shall have to see over the next few days," he said. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  FAILED" \par \par \uc2  Traders reported the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars after the real spiked higher to 2.075 per dollar in the afternoon, but said the support was a case of too little too late. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it didn't work," one trader said. "The market is testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...There is no doubt that it's serious." \par \par \uc2  The bank last confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November when it bought U.S. dollars and sold reais to redress a surge in the real following the country's biggest ever bank privatization. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Arminio Fraga has said he does not believe in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but that the bank will act in the case of a liquidity crunch. Traders criticized the bank's relaxed attitude to the real's slide. \par \par \uc2  "Their relaxed policy since January reached a critical point today which gives serious confidence to the players who were betting against the real to bet against it again," the trader said. "It's a classic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fight." \par \par \uc2  TRIPLE WHAMMY HITS REAL \par \par \uc2  Traders said the real was hit by concerns about the U.S. economic slowdown, worries ahead of a keenly-awaited Argentine economic announcement on Friday, and an explosion on Brazilian state oil giant Petrobras' biggest oil platform. \par \par \uc2  Fears about the extent of the downturn in the U.S. economy have been instrumental in wiping 7.4 percent off the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  Worries Argentina's dire straights would take the shine off Brazilian assets came to a head this week as the market was made to wait anxiously for new economy minister Ricardo Lopez Murphy to announce a plan to revive the moribund economy. \par \par \uc2  Officially denied rumors that Lopez Murphy was ready to resign just two weeks into his term and fears that legislators would put up tough opposition to his plan also weighed. \par \par \uc2  Explosions on the Petrobras platform, the world's biggest, weakened the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by raising fears the trade balance could suffer if Brazil had to buy more oil abroad. \par \par \uc2  "The trade balance is on sketchy ground as it is," said IDEAglobal market analyst Aryam Vasquez from New York. \par \par \uc2  The platform off the Rio de Janeiro coast was rocked by two explosions before daybreak, killing at least one person and threatening to sink the rig. The platform pumped 80,000 barrels of crude per day, five percent of Brazil's total. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3f03yzh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
