\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt,Buys Dlrs -Trader \b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 19:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in midafternoon trading Thursday to prop up the real after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossed the key psychological barrier of BRR2.10 per dollar a couple of hours earlier. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold millions of dollars, in a move that almost instantaneously strengthened the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to BRR2.0800 per dollar from a midrate of BRR2.1025 earlier. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected an estimated $400 million in the market, according to the local Estado news agency, based on information provided by various traders. \par \par \uc2  However, a Rio de Janeiro-based trader said it was impossible to tell at this point the amount of dollars sold by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can do this (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) through a number of dealers and any estimate that I make would be nothing more than a shot in the dark," said the trader. \par \par \uc2  The real, which ended at BRR2.076 Wednesday, had been weakening on broad concerns, including fears over the financial heath of neighboring Argentina and the U.S. economic slowdown. Earlier Thursday, the weakening was amplified by fears that Brazil will have to import more oil after two explosions halted production at the country's biggest oil rig. \par \par \uc2  Around 1840 GMT (1:40 p.m. EST), the real was changing hands at a midrate of BRR2.081 to the dollar, after hitting an intraday high of BRR2.074 shortly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move, traders don't expect the real to strengthen much further in coming days unless there's a dramatic improvement in the situation in Argentina. \par \par \uc2  "Investors will stay long on dollars (betting that the real will weaken) until things change in Argentina," said a Rio de Janeiro trader. \par \par \uc2  Newly appointed Argentine Economy Minister Ricardo Lopez Murphy is expected to announce measures Friday to revive that country's economy from three years of recession. \par \par \uc2  "Looks like it may be difficult to muster enough support to pass some key reforms there, and we're worried about it," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to confirm the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 2000 GMT (3:00 p.m. EST) when markets are closed. The bank usually says whether it sold or bought dollars, but often doesn't disclose the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount. A spokeswoman said bank had no immediate comment on the matter. \par \par \uc2  -By Adriana Arai and Anthony Dovkants, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11 3813-1988; adriana.arai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3f0146p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
