\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Mkt Debt Slumps As Nervous Market Eyes Argentina \b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 22:57\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- Emerging market debt players likely could use some relaxation on a beach, but probably not one in Argentina. \par \par \uc2  Debt prices got hit Thursday by mounting nervousness about Argentina's economic woes. The weakening of the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and continued volatility in U.S. stocks hardly helped the situation. \par \par \uc2  Reflecting the loss in confidence, the J.P. Morgan Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus, or EMBI+, cheapened around 14 basis points on the day to 754 basis points over U.S. Treasurys. \par \par \uc2  "People think it's better to be nervous and safe today than daring," a trader said. Price changes remained mainly dealer driven, due to the relative absence of investors in the marketplace as they wait for uncertain conditions to clear. \par \par \uc2  Argentina wound up as the most whipped for the day, cheapening around 42 basis points to 844 basis points over U.S. Treasurys. This wiped away many of the gains Argentina had won following the appointment of Ricardo Lopez Murphy as economy minister on March 5. \par \par \uc2  Jittery market players spread rumors Thursday that Lopez Murphy had already thrown in the towel on his challenging new job, even though the man in question had already denied such an accusation in Thursday's edition of La Nacion. \par \par \uc2  "The rumor about the resignation sounded weird to me," an investor said. Most New York-based market participants admitted that they didn't have enough information to make an educated guess about what was going on. \par \par \uc2  Market participants are eagerly awaiting the unveiling - expected to occur late Friday - of the economy minister's plan to cut government spending and improve tax collections in a bid to restore economic stability. \par \par \uc2  Argentina's woes didn't help neighboring Brazil, whose \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its lowest point in over two years, leading the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The real's weakness was amplified by fears that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade deficit will widen in coming months, after two explosions Thursday halted production indefinitely at a key oil rig off the coast of Rio de Janeiro. \par \par \uc2  Brazilian debt widened 16 basis points on the day. The Capitalization bond dropped to 79 bid from a closing price of around 80 bid on Wednesday, according to Maxemg.com. \par \par \uc2  In other market news Thursday, Mexico announced it would launch a new 2019 Global Bond of at least $1 billion to retire a portion of its outstanding Brady bond debt. The swap offer, which expires Mar. 22, is being managed by Credit Suisse First Boston and Salomon Smith Barney. \par \par \uc2  -By Sonja Ryst, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2245; sonja.ryst@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1179 1810 4071 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010711dx3f002x7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
