\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Brazil real ends at second weakest close ever. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Fabiola Girardin \par \uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 23:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 14 (Reuters) - Brazil's real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to its second weakest ever close on Wednesday after sharp losses on U.S. stock markets heightened worries about America's economic slowdown, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real softened to 2.078 per dollar from Tuesday's close of 2.063 per dollar. The only time the real closed weaker since it was introduced in mid-1994 was when it sank to 2.17 per dollar on March 2, 1999 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was devalued. \par \par \uc2  "The market is totally at the mercy of the United States and Argentina," said ING Barings trader Guilherme Abbud. \par \par \uc2  Argentina also weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as players waited nervously for newly appointed economy minister Ricardo Lopez Murphy to announce measures to get the neighboring economy out of its two and a half years of stagnation. \par \par \uc2  The real was under pressure from the word go as a lack of dollar offers and heightened fears that U.S. stock markets were going to fall out of bed knocked the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deep into two-year low territory. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. markets lived up to expectations. The Dow Jones Industrial average lost three percent and the technology-laden Nasdaq index dropped two percent. \par \par \uc2  The falls completely overshadowed a successful bond swap. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $2.15 billion in new 24-year global bonds allowing it to retire the same amount of Brady debt which both cuts the country's borrowing costs and frees up collateral that was tied to the old debt. \par \par \uc2  "The Brady swap didn't influence a thing," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Players also began to voice worries that the weakness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Brazilians' hunger for imports could lead to imported inflation which might threaten future interest rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  Official data released during the morning showed Brazil's IPCA inflation index, a key government gauge for setting interest rates, slowed to 0.46 percent in February, compared to 0.57 percent in January. \par \par \uc2  The IPCA consumer price index accelerated a cumulative 1.03 percent in the first two months of the year and 6.27 percent in the past 12 months. \par \par \uc2  But despite the inflation fears, players said they did not expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prop up the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Abbud said any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be viewed as "exaggerated". \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Arminio Fraga has said in the past that he does not believe in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the bank will act in the case of a liquidity crunch. \par \par \uc2  The bank last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in November buying U.S. dollars and selling reais to redress a surge in the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a major bank privatization. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3e03ur4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
