\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Calls It Transparency, Mkt Dubs It  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Terry Wade and Anthony Dovkants \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 835 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2001\par 21:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- They said they did it in the name of transparency, but the market dubbed it a case of  good old \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Top guns handling \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finances Thursday unveiled a two-year plan to buy a total $2.4 billion in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, or about $100 million each month. They said the aim is to make \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  more transparent. And analysts say that they have indeed achieved that goal. \par \par \uc2  But the announcement, which also sought to remove speculation about possible future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently said it would randomly buy up to $3 billion this year, came the morning after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sagged to its weakest point in 23 months. \par \par \uc2  The real strengthened on the back of the clarification and was standing at BRR1.997 against the dollar within 30 minutes of the start of trading, compared to Wednesday's close of BRR2.005. This came after senior officials paused their press conference to enable journalists to file the news ahead of the market's opening. \par \par \uc2  "Certainly, I think it was an attempt to pacify the market at the moment," said a Sao Paulo-based trader with an overseas investment bank. "But the fundamental problems still persist," he added. \par \par \uc2  Ultimately, it remains to be seen whether this morning's move will do any good for the real in the longer term this year. \par \par \uc2  Two traders said they wouldn't care to bet on just how long the real would bob just below the BRR2.00 level before weakening again as Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and equity markets continue to be hurt by worry about an unstable political scenario in Brasilia, a widening trade deficit - brought on by a robust local economy and a slowing U.S. economy - and an escalating trade dispute with Canada. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par       Will Dollar-Buying Plan Keep Real Strong?\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the buying plan will amount to about $5 million\par a day on the open market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That would give the real some strength, but probably not enough to\par beat the odds of further weakening.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But given an unusual confluence of factors, the real is probably going\par to slip more.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the country's rate of GDP growth is expected to hit 4.5% in 2001\par and surpass the rate of inflation for the first time in decades, the\par U.S. economy has slowed and oil prices remain high - two factors which\par are causing the trade deficit for Latin America's biggest economy to\par widen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "From the point of view of macroeconomic variables, indeed, it looks\par like the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is more likely to weaken than to strengthen through\par the end of the year," said Marcelo Carvalho, chief economist with JP\par Morgan in Sao Paulo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par And there is no fast way out of this dilemma. As the local economy\par heats up, Brazilians buy more imported luxury goods, creating further\par pressure on the trade deficit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "To narrow the trade deficit, Brazil could boost its exports and\par reduce the so-called Brazil risk, which would bring in foreign\par investment," said Carvalho.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some of Brazil's efforts to reduce its risk, however, are being\par delayed at the moment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Legislation to beef up shareholder rights rules and push through\par further fiscal reforms appear to be stalled in Congress as President\par Fernando Henrique Cardoso scrambles for a solution after a key party in\par his governing coalition walked away from him earlier this month.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Takes Another Step To Solidify Credibility\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Regardless of what happens to the real, no one doubts the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par Thursday went some way to further build its reputation, which has\par gradually improved since the clumsy early-1999 devaluation of the real.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think it (the announcement) really does clarify a misunderstanding\par that arose in the market last year about how much demand the treasury\par has for dollars," said David Roberts, economist at Banc Of America\par Securities in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This is one piece of a very long story of Brazilian monetary policy\par that's being moved towards a more predictable, transparent and\par consistent pattern," he added. "But you can't achieve such a goal all at\par once. It's all about credibility. This is something that is built and\par not just done in one announcement, but this is yet another step in that\par right direction."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The person credited with being the key architect behind much of the\par change is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  president Arminio Fraga.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Since his arrival in March 1999, the former George Soros fund manager\par has, among other steps, introduced minutes detailing the monthly\par interest rate meeting, set up an investor relations department and\par introduced a market report about demand for bonds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts credit Fraga with removing some of the mystery about\par Brazilian monetary policy. By 1900 GMT, the real stood at BRR1.991.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Terry Wade and Anthony Dovkants, Dow Jones Newswires;\par 55-11-3813-1988; brazil@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010725dx2800lep\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
