\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Brazil, Argentina to set common economic goals. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Gilbert Le Gras \par \uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 2000\par 02:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (updates with Buenos Aires Declaration details paras 4, 9, 13 and 14) \par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES, April 28 (Reuters) - Brazil and Argentina agreed on Friday to set common debt, deficit and inflation targets next March with a view to integrating six regional economies into an EU-like common market, ministers said. \par \par \uc2  "Next March we will have convergence targets," Brazilian Finance Minister Pedro Malan told reporters. "The idea is to keep inflation under control and ensure fiscal austerity." \par \par \uc2  Foreign, finance and defence ministers from South America's two largest nations met Thursday and Friday to forge closer trade, diplomatic and military ties to convert the Mercosur customs union into a European Union-style common market. \par \par \uc2  Among the 30 points of the so-called Buenos Aires Declaration is a resolution to eliminate intra-Mercosur nontariff barriers to trade by June 30, 2000. \par \par \uc2  Brazil and Argentina are members of the world's third largest trade bloc, which also includes Paraguay and Uruguay. Chile and Bolivia are associate members of the bloc that links 210 million people who produce $1 trillion in goods and services. \par \par \uc2  "We're seeking a common market with the free circulation of goods, services and people," said Brazilian Foreign Minister Luiz Felipe Lampreia. \par \par \uc2  Chile and Bolivia will be invited to talks aimed at setting common macroeconomic targets which would see the region's economies march at the same pace, said Argentine Economy Minister Jose Luis Machinea. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's more than 30 percent devaluation in January 1999 priced many Argentine exports out of the Brazilian market. The devaluation surprised Brazil's Mercosur partners and led to many trade disputes. \par \par \uc2  "We've also discussed the subject of setting up permanent (trade) tribunals," Argentine Foreign Minister Adalberto Rodriguez Giavarini said. Disputes have mostly been settled by political \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Argentina's presidents. \par \par \uc2  The declaration proposes "scaling back investment incentives to limit distortions" in the regional market. Argentine provincial governors often complain some Brazilian states offer large tax breaks to attract manufacturers. \par \par \uc2  Common economic goals should help keep those dangers in check and assure the region's economies move in sync. \par \par \uc2  Brazil and Argentina agreed to begin sharing debt, deficit and inflation statistics in September. This would serve as an early warning mechanism for potential future economic shocks. \par \par \uc2  Sharing data is a "fundamental step" to setting common debt, deficit and inflation targets, Brazil's Malan said, adding convergence would be achieved in years, not decades. \par \par \uc2  A bilateral macroeconomic monitoring group consisting of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance ministry officials will oversee the sharing of data and future adherence to the targets. Officials from the four other nations will be invited to join the body. \par \par \uc2  A task force will also work to detect money laundering. \par \par \uc2  The future deal has been dubbed "little Maastricht" due to its similarities to the EU's 1997 macroeconomic Maastricht Treaty which led to last year's creation of the euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Mercosur monetary union, however, may be a long way off with Argentina keener than Brazil. \par \par \uc2  Argentina has a matching amount of U.S. dollars in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for every peso in circulation to ensure its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is valued at a par with the greenback while Brazil's real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  floats freely on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Joint infrastructure, transport and energy projects to improve the flow of goods were discussed, Brazil's Malan said. \par \par \uc2  Argentine Industry Secretary Debora Giorgi said the partners agreed to study reducing Mercosur's common external tariff capital goods imports to improve regional productivity. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4t01s6q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
