\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Ctrl Bk Confirms  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  On  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market Fri \b0\par\par\uc2 166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 21:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - - 24/03/00 20-44G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2044GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Friday confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during Friday's session. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't say whether it sold or purchased dollars, nor the amount or exchange rate involved in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, market participants said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came into the market early in the session, buying anywhere between $5 million and $100 million. Traders said it marks the first time since the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was devalued in January 1999 that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As reported, the real closed trading at a midrate of 1.733 reals (BRR)\par per dollar, after testing the BRR1.70/dollar barrier just after the\par opening bell. The real hasn't closed below BRR1.70 since May 24.\par -By Adriana Arai and Stephen Wisnefski; Dow Jones Newswires; (5511)\par 813-1988; stephen.wisnefski@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3o01jzz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex