\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Real Opens -2: All Eyes On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2000\par 12:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO -(Dow Jones)- The Brazilian real opened stronger against the dollar Monday, on optimism over Brazil's economic recovery, leaving traders wondering how much further the government will allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Brazilian real opened at a midrate of BRR1.7675 to the dollar on a spread of BRR1.7660 to BRR1.7690 per dollar, compared with a close of BRR1.7725 to the dollar Friday on a tighter spread of BRR1.7720 to BRR1.7730 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "People are wondering how long the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will allow this to go on," said a Rio de Janeiro based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader, referring to the rally in the real since November, which has brought the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its strongest level in 6 months. \par \par \uc2  Traders are speculating that the government doesn't favor a real which is any stronger than BRR1.7500/dlr, as this will hurt \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports. \par \par \uc2  Some expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by buying dollars if the real reaches this level, while others expect the bank to attempt to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by reducing the amount of dollar linked papers which it offers to the market to roll over existing positions, thus creating more liquidity in reals. \par \par \uc2  "On the other hand, it could be that the market itself takes profits when it reaches BRR1.7500, given that everyone expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop it from going beyond this level," said another Rio de Janeiro based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily average, known as Ptax, which forms the basis for all forward contracts, stood at BRR1.7780 per dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Ben Backwell; Dow Jones Newswires; 5521-580-9394;\par     benjamin.backwell@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dj00000020010805dw1o00cjt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
