\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's real ends firmer at 1.815 per dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2000\par 20:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Jan 10 (Reuters) - Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the real\tab  , ended stronger Monday as a favourable outlook for Latin America's largest economy overshadowed concerns over rising U.S. interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The real finished 0.7 percent firmer at 1.815 per dollar, boosted by dollars that flowed into the country on the back of a calmer market setting, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "The dollar inflows that began in the morning continued throughout the day," one local trader said. \par \par \uc2  "Economic indicators are looking brighter this year," said another, underlining the capital inflows. Economists were pointing to more foreign direct investment, positive growth and stable inflation among other things this year. \par \par \uc2  The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had weakened last week, in line with a crumbling stock market, as investors watched Wall Street shares drop amid concerns over rising U.S. interest rates. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling dollars to calm investors and help the real turn around from a weak point of 1.850 per dollar reached on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  While recovering from last week's losses, the real, at 1.815, was still 33 percent weaker compared to its pre-devaluation level one year ago. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5423)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1a03mah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\pic