\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real firms at open after Cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2000\par 13:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Jan 5 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab   firmed slightly at Wednesday's opening with traders leery that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again as it did on Tuesday to sell dollars and support the local unit, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The real started trading at 1.848 per dollar, 0.11 percent stronger than its previous close of 1.850.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "After the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was able to reduce the slide of the (local) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, everyone is going to be careful today," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  The real had weakened 2.14 percent to 1.860 per dollar on Tuesday before the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in. \par \par \uc2  The weakness came as speculators played on growing fears of a possible credit tightening in the United States, which could slow an expected influx of investment dollars into emerging markets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The slide yesterday was exaggerated and reflected the hysteria of the market in relation to the fears of a rise in rates in the U.S.," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  He downplayed the situation saying a U.S. hike should have been put in effect last month, but had been put off because of nervousness about problems from the millennium computer bug. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve meets on Feb. 1-2 to define its monetary policy with regards to the basic interest rate, which now stands at 5.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((Rio de Janeiro newsroom +55 21 223 7142, rio.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1507yjp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
