\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Seen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  To Support Real \b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2000\par 19:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Tuesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling dollars to support the Brazilian real, traders said. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman was not immediately able to confirm the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , citing the bank's normal practice of confirming any such action after the trading day has ended. \par \par \uc2  According to dealers, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to BRR1.8600 per dollar, from Monday's close of BRR1.8200. The real strengthened to BRR1.8490 per dollar on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The real has weakened over the last two days on fears that a hike in U.S. interest rates may be in the offing. \par \par \uc2  The real ended 1999 with its highest close of six months at BRR1.8050 per dollar, and strengthened more than 6% in December alone, although it is still more than 30% weaker than its pre-devaluation level of BRR1.21 per dollar in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  -By Ben Backwell; Dow Jones Newswires; (5521) 580 9394; \par \par \uc2  -benjamin.backwell@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw14002ze\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
