\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Real Ends At BRR1.811/Dlr Vs BRR1.807 End Fri. \b0\par\par\uc2 244 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 1999\par 20:50\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  BRASILIA -(Dow Jones)- The Brazilian real (BRR) ended slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar Monday in thin volume, as early inflows dried up in the afternoon amid end-of-year market slack, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real closed at a midrate of BRR1.811 to the dollar on a tight spread of BRR1.810-1.812 per dollar, compared with Friday's closing mark of BRR1.807 to the dollar on an equally narrow spread. Monday morning, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had hit a five-month intra-day high at BRR1.795 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Liquidity is pretty dry now at the end of the year, so any small inflow or outflow will move the market" said a Rio de Janeiro-based trader. \par \par \uc2  "We had more inflows in the morning, to the real got stronger, but then there were a little more outflows in the afternoon and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened," the same trader said, adding that the market believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the real if it hits BRR1.82. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's foreign reserves stood at $41.519 billion Friday, up from\par Thursday's $41.396 billion level. Daily international reserves figures\par are available at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's web page:\par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bcb.gov.br/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bcb.gov.br}}}\uc2 \f2 , with a\par one-day lag.\par    -By Adriana Arai; Dow Jones Newswires;\par  55-61 9965-6883 or 321-1224 (adriana.arai@dowjones.com)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Doku