\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Central Bk Comes Full Circle In Real's Defense \b0\par\par\uc2  By Stephen Wisnefski \par \uc2 1,292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 1999\par 16:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come full circle over the past year and is once again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But unlike last December and early January, when the real was attacked by speculators and dollars fled the country in droves, this time around the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have its back up against the wall. \par \par \uc2  "These are basically technical \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to inject some liquidity when needed. Before the real was devalued, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no choice but to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to keep the real within its trading band, said Carlos Augusto Levorim, director at Oryx Asset Management in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling small amounts now, and only doing so when they know the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  will work," he added, praising the skills of central banker Arminio Fraga, who took the reigns at the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  six times in the past five weeks, most recently on Monday. In the process, the real (BRR) has strengthened to BRR1.8615 per dollar, from BRR1.9420 at the start of November. \par \par \uc2  Many market participants expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen further, to around BRR1.80/dollar by year-end. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't trying to artificially strenghten (the real) with these \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but rather trying to minimize excessive volatility from compromising inflation goals and (fiscal) targets," said Carlos Geraldo Langoni, director of the Getulio Vargas Foundation's center for World Economics and a former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president. \par \par \uc2  When Brazil decided to float its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in mid-January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as necessary to contain brusque movements in the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  As the months passed, Brazil moved dangerously close to the floor for international reserves stipulated in an agreement with the International Monetary Fund, generating concerns the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was helpless to defend the real as it tested the BRR2.00/dollar barrier. \par \par \uc2  The more frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of late were made possible by a revised agreement with the IMF in late October, which lowered the floor of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, giving the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  an extra $2 billion in ammunition to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Observers agree that the spate of recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  typically spends less than $100 million, doesn't imply the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a specific exchange rate target, as some have charged. \par \par \uc2  "It appears that the psychological barrier of BRR2.00 was something the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't comfortable with," said Dalton Gardimam, senior economist at CLSA in Sao Paulo. "But if (officials) had a formal or informal target in mind, they would be much more aggressive than they've been." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market Optimism About 2000 Makes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Viable\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par What differentiates today's scenario from a year ago is that the\par potential weakness of the real appears to be a temporary phenomenon,\par with Brazilian debt obligations bunched up at the end of the year. The\par country has around $3 billion in debt payments coming due this month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said that even if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wasn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par regularly, there's no reason to believe the real would weaken\par significantly because market optimism about the prospects for 2000 is\par running high.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Brazil's trade accounts are expected to show a significant improvement\par next year, which will help reduce a current account deficit that hovers\par around 4% of gross domestic product.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par According to the revised terms of the IMF deal announced last week,\par Brazil should show a trade surplus of $5 billion in 2000, down from an\par expected $1.5 billion deficit this year. It's also seen reducing its\par current account deficit to $22.5 billion next year, from $26 billion in\par 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is completely convinced outflows will be much\par lower in the first half of 2000, the recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are just\par designed to smooth the process," said CLSA's Gardimam.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If you believed the real would weaken significantly, you'd just be\par throwing dollars away," he added. "We believe the improvement in the\par scenario is coming, so (the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) are justified."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Added another former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  director who now works at a leading\par local investment bank: "The good thing now is that, with relatively few\par resources, you can stabilize the market."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Given the expected improvement in the country's current accounts -\par which continue being completely financed by huge foreign direct\par investment - there's no reason to allow the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken\par significantly and possibly threaten inflation targets, added former\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  head Langoni.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Brazilian consumer prices are now expected to rise about 8.5% this\par year, well below initial post-devaluation forecasts. And the government\par projects the rate will fall to around 6% next year and 4% in 2001.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "With the improved trade performance, a better international scenario\par and calmer political situation here, there's no reason to have such a\par weak real," Langoni said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He added that he expects the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par until \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  starts showing monthly trade surpluses on a consistent\par basis, which he predicted won't happen until the second quarter of 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Current Account Situation Remains Big Threat\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Aside from the periodic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also\par helped strengthen the real the past few days by auctioning dollars to\par investors willing to sell them back in January, as part of a strategy to\par increase liquidity in the transition to the year 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last Friday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $800 million. The bank announced\par late Monday it will offer another $500 million this coming Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "These are just necessary moves. No \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the world can\par afford to do nothing about Y2K," CLSA's Gardimam said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While there's consensus the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's actions on the exchange\par market are the right moves in the short term, Brazil may not be out of\par the woods entirely.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some observers point out that the government isn't paying enough\par attention to the potential hazards associated with the huge current\par account deficit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We have an exchange rate that isn't sufficient to bring the current\par account gap down to a level that is sustainable over time," said the\par former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official who asked to remain anonymous.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the exchange rate would probably have to remain above\par BRR2.00/dollar to effect a serious improvement of the current account.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "What makes me nervous about the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  situation is that the current\par account deficit is still 4% of GDP, and we have a huge internal debt\par stock that is dollar-linked," he added, pegging that debt at about $50\par billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the internal debt stock is lower now than it was at the start of\par the year, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has continuously sold dollar-linked debt this\par year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official acknowledged, however, that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't in a position now to allow the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par weaken.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has to keep the real within a range that doesn't\par affect inflation and doesn't compromise the economic policy of the\par government," he said. "In many ways, the exchange rate is a barometer of\par economic policy."\par -By Stephen Wisnefski; Dow Jones Newswires; (5511) 813-1988;\par stephen.wisnefski@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Corrected 1713GMT)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't trying to artificially strengthen (the real)\par with these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but rather trying to minimize excessive\par volatility from compromising inflation goals and (fiscal) targets," said\par Carlos Geraldo Langoni, director of the Getulio Vargas Foundation's\par center for World Economics and a former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  president.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (In the item "Brazil's Central Bk Comes Full Circle In Real's\par Defense," published around 1558 GMT, Langoni was incorrectly quoted as\par saying "straighten" instead of "strengthen".)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1106 1838 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvc708c00\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
