\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real opens firmer, mkts bet on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 1999\par 13:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Dec 7 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab   opened even firmer Tuesday after hitting a four-month high Monday as investors bet on further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The real kicked off at 1.859 per dollar, 0.48 percent stronger from its Monday close of 1.868, which was the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strongest level since Aug. 11.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "With the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supplying dollars the way it is doing now, the dollar can only weaken," said one trader at a foreign bank in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday sold dollars in the market for the second time this month to ease tight supply on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a heavy corporate debt financing schedule of about $4 billion in December. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in the market four times in November, helping to bring the real off its seven-month lows near the 2-for-1 dollar threshold. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5423)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc708so8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
