\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real opens firmer on cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1999\par 13:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Nov 18 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab   opened slightly firmer on Thursday at 1.929 per dollar, compared with Wednesday's close of 1.931, a day after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold dollars, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "With the cenbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday, nobody is ruling out another \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  today," a local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader said. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pulled the real back from a low of 1.939 with its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the day before.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold dollars a couple of times since October when it lowered its minimum requirement for international reserves and beefed up the supply of dollars with loans and bonds. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, foreign reserves jumped $1.12 billion with inflows from an international loan, part of the $41.5 billion bailout agreed with the International Monetary Fund last November. \par \par \uc2  The real has lost 37 percent of its value since capital flight forced Brazil to devalue in mid-January. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5408)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbi09sq3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\p