\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Fin Min: \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Best Way To Limit Inflation \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1999\par 21:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BRASILIA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry Economic Policy Secretary Edward Amadeo said the best strategy to ward off the inflationary pressures of late are \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than hiking interest rates, the local Estado news agency reported Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "This (recent) inflation wasn't triggered by excess demand," he told Estado in an exclusive interview. "That's why hiking rates would be worthless," he was quoted as saying. \par \par \uc2  Amadeo said in November inflation won't be as high as in October. He argued that 90% of the higher-than-expected 1.19% October inflation as measured by the IPCA index came from transitory factors such as price hikes for cars, alcohol fuel, and meat. \par \par \uc2  However, the FGV research institute released earlier Thursday a higher-than-expected inflation figure for the Oct. 21 to Nov. 20 period, at 1.87%. \par \par \uc2  This index, called IGP-M, is a broad measure of consumer, wholesale and construction costs, and had been pegged at around 1.5% by economists. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market selling dollars twice this month and once in October as the real (BRR) trod dangerous BRR1.95-BRR2.00/per dollar territory. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closed at BRR1.929dlr, compared to Wednesday's\par close of BRR1.93/dlr.\par  -