\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens -2: Market Wary On Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1999\par 12:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO -(Dow Jones)- The Brazilian real opened unchanged against the dollar Thursday, with market participants cautious after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real opened at a midrate of BRR1.9300 to the dollar, on a wide spread of BRR1.9280 to BRR1.9320 per dollar, compared to Wednesday's closing midrate of BRR1.9300 per dollar, on a tighter spread of BRR1.9290 to BRR1.9310 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is taking a very active stance at the moment," said a Rio de Janeiro-based trader. "Nobody is going to make a big speculative play against the real in these conditions," he added. \par \par \uc2  Late Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the real, after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to BRR1.9390 per dollar on rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary-policy committee or Copom, was holding an extraordinary meeting. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied the rumors, and its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon pushed the real to BRR1.9290 per dollar, before closing at BRR1.9300 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that the market will be watching closely the release later Thursday of inflation data from the privately run Getulio Vargas Institute. \par \par \uc2  Market participants are expecting the IGP-M index projection for November to come in at 1.6%, but some speak of a figure as high as 2%. \par \par \uc2  As reported, consumer prices rose 1.19% in October, compared with a 0.31% increase the previous month, according to the IPCA consumer price index, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses as its official measure of inflation. \par \par \uc2  In the first ten months of the year, the IPCA index showed inflation of 7.27%. The Brazilian government has a target for inflation, as measured by the IPCA, of less than 8% in 1999. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to sell BRR1 billion in fixed rate LTN papers later Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily average rate - known as the Ptax - was BRR1.9323 per dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Ben Backwell; Dow Jones Newswires; (5521) 580-9394;\par     benjamin.backwell@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dj00000020010827dvbi07dcj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
