\par\par \b \uc2  Bradys:Brazil Drags Market Down On Inflation,  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Worries \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 1999\par 22:17\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- Brazilian bonds led emerging market securities lower Wednesday on investor concerns that inflationary pressures could soon drag down the economy of the Latin giant. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's Capitalization bonds dropped 1 1/2 to 69 bid after \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up a weakening real. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the real began to weaken on rumors - later denied by the government - that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee was holding an extraordinary meeting to further hike interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "People don't like to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and we saw a little nervousness," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  The yield spread of the J.P. Morgan's Emerging Market Bond Index widened by about 0.11 percentage point over Treasurys. The spread of the benchmark index narrowed almost 100 basis points in the last few weeks as investors returned to emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  "I think the demand for paper in the last month has surprised a lot of people," a New York trader said. \par \par \uc2  With some investors now wondering whether the end of a recent rally is in sight, traders said some bondholders have begun to take profits. \par \par \uc2  "It's not clear whether this is a consolidation or whether the rally is cresting," said Francis Rodilosso, an emerging market debt trader at Credit Lyonnais in New York. \par \par \uc2  Argentine bonds also came under pressure, with the Floating-Rate Bonds down more than a point to 88 bid. \par \par \uc2  "The new supply didn't help the market," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  After reopening its Global bonds due 2017 on Monday, Argentina is once again tapping the Eurobond market with a EUR300 million offering of new 10% securities due Dec. 7, 2004. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, two other Latin American nations priced bonds Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Colombia placed $500 million of new 10-year bonds at 92.773 to yield\par 11.593%. The notes are putable in 2005. If investors elect not to put,\par the bonds will turn into Colombia's outstanding 2009 Eurobonds. Also,\par Mexico priced Y30 billion of 3.0% four-year samurai bonds at Y100.31.\par -By Carol S. Remond; Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2074\par -carol.remond@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1179 1810 4071 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010827dvbh005i5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
