\par\par \b \uc2  Latin America  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Namju Cho \par \uc2 468 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 1999\par 21:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The Brazilian real finished sharply stronger against the U.S. dollar Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Mexican peso also gained against the U.S. dollar on the back of a positive economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  The Brazilian real opened at BRR1.931 to the dollar, and later slipped to BRR1.939, at which point the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to news agency Estado. \par \par \uc2  The move follows an earlier \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Nov. 10, when the bank sold dollars when the real weakened to about BRR1.95. \par \par \uc2  The real closed stronger at BRR1.929 to the dollar, compared with Monday's close of BRR1.932. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sending a clear signal that it will not let the real weaken beyond certain levels," one U.S.-based trader said. \par \par \uc2  The trader noted that the real's level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been growing stronger every time. \par \par \uc2  The bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  back in August for the first time in many months, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly broke the psychologically-important BRR2.00-level. \par \par \uc2  The real dipped below BRR2.00 in late October, however, prompting the bank to again sell dollars. Then the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Nov. 10 when the real weakened to around BRR1.95. \par \par \uc2  The trader said the bank's move was a prudent one to contain inflation, which has been on the rise. "The bank doesn't want to allow \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to put pressure on inflation," he said. A weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  leads to higher import prices and could possibly create inflationary pressures. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Mexican peso continued to strengthen on consistently positive sentiment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Mexican peso closed at MXN9.332, compared with Tuesday's close of MXN9.381. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, smaller Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed. \par \par \uc2  The Colombian peso strengthened to CLP1,941 against the dollar Wednesday, boosted by significant dollar sales by the country's treasury, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  Colombia's treasury is set to bring into Colombia hundreds of millions of international financing dollars by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  Below is a summary of regional exchange rates in late trading compared to one U.S. dollar: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                           Wednesday(Close)    Tuesday(Close)\par Brazilian real (BRR)           1.9290             1.9320\par Mexican peso (MXN)             9.3320             9.3810\par Venezuelan bolivar (VEB)     634.5000           633.7500\par Peruvian sol (PEN)             3.4736             3.4750\par Ecuadorean sucre (ECS)    18,300.0000 *      18,000.0000\par Colombian peso (COP)       1,941.0000         1,958.0000\par Chilean peso (CLP)           540.7000           538.6000\par    *1800 GMT\par    Note: Argentine Peso is fixed 1:1 against the U.S. dollar under a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board regime.\par -By Namju Cho; Dow Jones Newswires, 201-938-5692,\par namju.cho@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1093 1835 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvbh07zm9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
