\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real ends firmer on suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 207 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1999\par 20:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Nov 10 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab   ended firmer at 1.929 per dollar Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  apparently \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market, buying dollars and taking pressure off the real, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The real strengthened 0.4 percent after starting the day much weaker at 1.947 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market early in the session to back up the real amid expectations there would be more capital flight pressuring the real. \par \par \uc2  "It was enough for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to show its face," said one local trader. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not confirm the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and a spokesperson said the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only comment after the market closed. \par \par \uc2  The real had finished the previous three sessions weaker as dollar outflows from the market and profit-taking on recent gains capped its strength. \par \par \uc2  Trading at 1.929 per dollar, the real was still 37 percent weaker below its pre-devaluation levels in mid-January. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters Tuesday forecast the real would settle on the strong side of the two-per-dollar barrier as it enters the next millennium. \par \