\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real up after suspected C.Bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1999\par 13:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Nov 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped sharply to 1.934 per dollar in early trade after opening much lower, at 1.947 to the greenback, following apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market selling dollars this morning. It is difficult to say how much it sold, but it had a big psychological effect. Few people want to buy dollars now," said a Rio de Janeiro-based trader with a major bank, who did not want to be identified. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not deny or confirm the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A spokesman told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only comment after the market closure on Wednesday. The bank said last month it had a wide poool of reserves to help the real. \par \par \uc2  The real finished Tuesday at 1.937 per dollar, tad weaker than on Monday as dollar outflows from the market and profit-taking on recent gains capped its strength. \par \par \uc2  Traders had been expecting more outflows on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Trading at 1.937 to the dollar, the Brazilian real is 37.5 percent weaker than before its devaluation in mid-January. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters forecast Tuesday the real should settle on the strong side of the two-per-dollar barrier as it enters the next millennium. \par \par \uc2  ((Andrei Khalip, Sao Paulo newsroom 55 11 248 5532)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Li