\par\par \b \uc2  Latin America  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Namju Cho \par \uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1999\par 21:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones) --The Brazilian real gained against the U.S. dollar Wednesday after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets, for the first time in two weeks, to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Mexican peso also gained strength as market participants were unwinding long dollar positions following strong U.S. wholesale data released Wednesday, which prompted inflationary fears. \par \par \uc2  The real opened at BRR1.939 to the dollar, and weakened to BRR1.945, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to call banks inquiring about spreads on the real, according to local traders. \par \par \uc2  The real soon hit BRR1.933 and strengthened further to close at a midrate of BRR1.928, compared with Tuesday's close of BRR1.935. \par \par \uc2  As reported earlier, the bank confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  but gave no further details. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move puzzled one U.S.-based trader, as the real hadn't weakened sharply. The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real had broken the psychologically important BRR2.00-level. \par \par \uc2  "The only explanation I can find is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to be preemptive" ahead of the U.S. Federal Open Committee Meeting Nov. 16, he said. \par \par \uc2  In the event a Fed rate hike causes \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the board to fall drastically, the real would be weakening from a higher level, he said. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials are expected to slice the benchmark Selic interest rate target by about 50 basis points from its current level of 19% later Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  After peaking in March at 45%, the bank has been steadily reducing the Selic. \par \par \uc2  While bullish on the real, Lehman Brothers said in a report earlier this week that "the principal risks to the real include potential delays of fiscal legislation" to reduce its fiscal deficit. \par \par \uc2  Similarly, the Mexican peso also edged up against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Mexican peso opened stronger at MXN9.433 and closed at the same level. The peso closed at MXN9.435 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The trader said market participants had "caught themselves long dollars" after core U.S. wholesale prices for October came out higher than expected and reignited inflationary concerns. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, smaller Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were weaker against the greenback. \par \par \uc2  The Ecuadorean sucre closed 2.5% lower against the dollar Wednesday at ECS17,200 in active trading as market participants continued buying dollars to cover debts in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , local traders said. \par \par \uc2  They added that market participants were awaiting an agreement to be signed between the government and the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  Ecuador is currently trying to restructure more than $6 billion in debt with bondholders but hasn't made much progress after its first day of meetings with creditors Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Ecuador's finance minister, Alfredo Arizaga, said Wednesday that the sucre will be around ECS14,500 per dollar by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  The Colombian peso weakened to COP1,954 to the dollar despite significant inflows of oil and coffee dollars, due to a major purchase of dollars executed shortly before market close, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  Below is a summary of regional exchange rates in late trading compared to one U.S. dollar: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                          Wednesday(Close) Tuesday(Close)\par Brazilian real (BRR)           1.9280             1.9350\par Mexican peso (MXN)             9.4330             9.4350\par Venezuelan bolivar (VEB)     632.5000           632.0000\par Peruvian sol (PEN)             3.4832             3.4820\par Ecuadorean sucre (ECS)    17,200.0000        16,775.0000\par Colombian peso (COP)       1,954.0000         1,952.5000\par Chilean peso (CLP)           542.5000           541.8000\par    *1845 GMT\par    Note: Argentine Peso is fixed 1:1 against the U.S. dollar under a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board regime.\par    -By Namju Cho; Dow Jones Newswires, 201-938-5692,\par namju.cho@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1093 1835 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvba07wil\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
