\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Central Bk Says It  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market Wed \b0\par\par\uc2 117 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1999\par 20:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but provided no details on the move. \par \par \uc2  It marked the first time in two weeks that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The real (BRR) opened weaker against the dollar Wednesday, following the release of disappointing inflation figures late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  After weakening to BRR1.9450 per dollar, market participants said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began calling banks and asking for spreads on the real, suggesting an imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. Next, the real strengthened to BRR1.9330. \par \par \uc2  The real closed trading at BRR1.9280. \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvba07wfv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
