\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  seen cutting rates Wednesday. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carlos Dias \par \uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 1999\par 18:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Nov 9 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could reap the benefits of a series of steps to bolster its real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cut interest rates Wednesday when its policy-setting Copom committee meets, economists said. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll of 20 economists this week found 14 respondents predicting a rate cut of at least 0.25 percentage point in the benchmark Selic reference rate, currently at 19 percent. \par \par \uc2  "I think there is a combination of factors favouring a rate reduction, like declining inflationary pressures and improvements in the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Carlos Kawall, an economist at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  He predicted half a percentage point cut. \par \par \uc2  At its last meeting October 6, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Committee (Copom) made no rate change, but adopted a bias to lower rates in the future. \par \par \uc2  At the time, Brazil's financial markets and the real were slumping as the government struggled to restore confidence after a court ruling slashed some 2.4 billion reais in expected revenues for 2000 from higher pension contributions. \par \par \uc2  But since then, the government has moved aggressively to change the law governing pensions and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has worked hard to steady the real. \par \par \uc2  In the last two weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced two important policy changes - an increase in the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves it can use to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and steps to overhaul \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's huge domestic debt market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's measures have been cheered by the markets and the real has strengthened. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officially only targets inflation in setting rates. But a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen as a harbinger of imported inflation, so the real's recovery has opened the door to lower rates. \par \par \uc2  Price rises have remained modest since Brazil devalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has an inflation target of 8 percent for this year, measured by the Brazilian Institute of Geography and Statistics' IPCA inflation index. From January to September, cumulative price rises came to only 6.01 percent. \par \par \uc2  Everything is working in the direction of a rate cut, said Dany Rappaport, chief economist at Banco Santander in Sao Paulo, who predicts a 25-basis-point cut in the Selic rate. "The fundamentals are ready, the foreign and fiscal accounts are improving." \par \par \uc2  The government's response to the court ruling has been to send a constitutional amendment to Congress. The bill is currently at the committee stage. \par \par \uc2  Specifically, the amendment aims to overturn the part of the constitution stipulating that retired civil servants cannot be required to make pension contributions even if their pensions are as high as their previous wages. The Supreme Court ruled that forcing retired pensioners to pay in was unconstitutional. \par \par \uc2  The results of the Reuters poll found seven economists predicting a 25-basis-point cut, and five forecasting a 50-basis-point cut. One economist expected a 100-basis-point cut, and another a 30-basis-point cut. The remaining six saw no change in rates Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Brasilia Newsroom, +55-61-314-1193)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvb900df2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
