\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Has Additional $2 Billion For  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1999\par 21:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BRASILIA -(Dow Jones)- A revised agreement between \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the International Monetary Fund gives the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  an extra $2 billion in ammunition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market defending the real, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Arminio Fraga said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The extra funds derive from a lower floor for net international reserves that the Brazilian government managed to negotiate with the IMF during a two-week visit of Fund economists that ended earlier this week. This was the fourth time the two sides reworked the terms of a $41.5 billion aid package assembled in November 1998. \par \par \uc2  The new floor for net international reserves - which excludes money received from the IMF - at the end of November is $20.99 billion. With this new floor, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have $4.18 billion to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Fraga said the figure is net of Treasury foreign commitments and possible new bond issues, which would raise this limit. \par \par \uc2  At the end of December, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees net international reserves at $23.5 billion, or $3.23 billion above the new $20.30 billion floor set for year-end. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday for the first time in more than two months, as the real (BRR) broke through the BRR2.00/barrier for the second time in as many weeks. \par \par \uc2  Speaking at the same news conference, monetary policy director Luiz Fernando Figueiredo declined to comment on how much the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected in the market Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Fraga attributed recent pressure on the real to market anxiety relative to the previous international reserve floor and a seasonal concentration of bond maturities, including Treasury notes. \par \par \uc2  The central banker said the process of institutions moving forward their foreign debt payments because of concerns about how close Brazil was to the floor should stop, adding that the $2 billion extra \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  margin is a "comfortable, convenient level given the current market conditions." \par \par \uc2  Fraga said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  negotiated more funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a precaution to ensure that inflation targets will be met. \par \par \uc2  "We don't have direct concern about the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate," he said, but he noted that if the real continues to weaken, it could drive up inflation. \par \par \uc2  Fraga said the funds exceeding the floor at the end of this year may also be used to cover gaps in the balance of payments, "if needed." \par \par \uc2  Officials declined Thursday to provide new forecasts for the balance of payments this year. \par \par \uc2  Fraga noted that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  also negotiated extra \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds for the year 2000. \par \par \uc2  For January, the new IMF floor for net international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves has been set at $18.95 billion, with funds available for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen at $4.70 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  For February, the floor is $19.75 billion, with available \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds seen at $4.45 billion. The floor for March has been set at $21.35 billion, giving \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  $2.41 billion for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Fraga stressed that these figures are net of new bond issues, "which will likely take place." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The full details of the revised IMF package are scheduled to be\par released next week.\par    -By Adriana Arai; Dow Jones Newswires\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Copyright (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All Rights Reserved.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020330dvas009zw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
