\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Opens -2: Caution After Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1999\par 13:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO -(Dow Jones)- The Brazilian real opened slightly stronger against the dollar Thursday with the market cautious after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Wednesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The Brazilian real opened at a midrate of BRR1.9830 per dollar on a wide spread of BRR1.9810 to BRR1.9850, compared with Wednesday's close of BRR1.9880 per dollar on a spread of BRR1.9870 to BRR1.9890 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody really knows what the new rules are," said a Rio de Janeiro trader, referring to a new accord with the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  "Does the new agreement with the IMF give the bank freedom to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a defined period or at a defined level, and how much is it permitted to run down reserves?", he added. \par \par \uc2  A Finance Ministry official said Wednesday the IMF and Brazil had reached an agreement that would change existing rules for the floor of Brazil's international reserves, allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more flexibility to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The agreement has yet to be formalized, and details will be released late next week. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, selling dollars to several financial institutions, as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to below the 2.00 reals per dollar psychological barrier. \par \par \uc2  As part of a $41.5 billion IMF-led international aid package introduced last November, the Brazilian government agreed not to allow foreign reserves to slip below $22 billion, excluding more than $18 billion in aid received. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's foreign reserves were $39.934 billion Tuesday, compared with $39.921 billion the previous day. \par \par \uc2  "All that we know is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from going beyond BRR2.0 (per dollar)," said another Rio trader. "We don't know how solid a base there is behind this policy." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will offer BRR3 billion in fixed rate LTN papers later Thursday and BRR1.5 billion in floating rate LFT's. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily average rate - known as the Ptax - was BRR1.9950 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Beginning Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to publish its official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate every half hour during trading hours, instead of simply publishing the Ptax at the end of the day. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Ben Backwell, Dow Jones Newswires;\par (5521)580-9394; ben.backwell@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvas07n0q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
