\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's real firms on slew of cenbank measures. \b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1999\par 21:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Oct 28 (Reuters) - Brazil's real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab   closed 0.75 percent firmer on Thursday at 1.974 per dollar, helped by a slew of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  measures, including a possible strengthening of the bank's dollar \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pool, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The dollar fell here because of an inflow of dollars caused by a bunch of good news," said one trader.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Arminio Fraga said Thursday Brazil was discussing with the International Monetary Fund (IMF) to cut the floor for the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $2 billion, which would give \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  more flexibility to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Fraga said pressure on the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks have been motivated by a large amount of foreign debt payments coming due and "a wrong perception that we don't have flexibility," in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Wednesday, helping the real spring back from under the psychological two-reais-per-dollar mark. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said Thursday it was scrapping limits on banks' short \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market positions in a move to free up liquidity in the market and allowing banks to sell more dollars. \par \par \uc2  Further, the market warmed to Brazil's successful sovereign bond issue of 500 million euros. The government had initially placed 300 million euros, but increased the size in just a few hours on the back of good market reception. \par \par \uc2  The real has now firmed two days in a row, but was still 38.7 percent weaker compared to its pre-devaluation level in January. \par \par \uc2  ((Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5423)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvas013k4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
