\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil set to cut floor of foreign reserve levels. \b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1999\par 20:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRASILIA, Oct 28 (Reuters) - Brazil is negotiating with the International Monetary Fund (IMF) to cut the projected floor for the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $2 billion, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Arminio Fraga said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The new levels will give \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  more flexibility to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will create a new floor for projected foreign reserves in December of $20.3 billion. \par \par \uc2  Government officials said earlier this week the government was renegotiating the foreign reserves requirements agreed with the IMF under the terms of a $41.5 billion international loan deal. \par \par \uc2  Under the deal, foreign reserves levels are projected for every month, with an allowed deviance level of $3 billion, and a year-end target for reserves of $26.3 billion. The new agreement announced Thursday will simply lower those levels. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Arminio Fraga said the projected level for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at the end of the year will now be $23.532 billion, while the allowed floor will be $20.3 billion. \par \par \uc2  At the end of November, reserve levels are projected to stand at $25.173 billion, and there will be a minimum allowed floor of $20.99 billion. \par \par \uc2  The reserve levels targeted with the IMF exclude disbursements from the loan deal. \par \par \uc2  Fraga said pressure on the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks have been motivated by a large amount of foreign debt payments coming due and "a wrong perception that we don't have flexibility," in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Wednesday, helping the real firm up a bit. \par \par \uc2  ((Brasilia Newsroom, +55-61-314-1193)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvas0128n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
