\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil stocks up with Wall St, helped by local news. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrei Khalip \par \uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 1999\par 00:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Oct 28 (Reuters) - Brazilian stocks rose in tandem with Wall Street on Thursday, boosted by the successful launch of a 7-year euro bond and by a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  promise to set aside more money to back the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders only singled out Telesp telecommunications company, whose preferred stock rose 5.5 percent following an announcement the firm had set up a telephony services unit. \par \par \uc2  "Telesp has been undervalued for a while compared to other companies in the sector," said Felipe Padua, portfolio manager with Banco Opportunity in Rio de Janeiro. \par \par \uc2  "All other stocks rose almost indiscriminately on a general market upturn," said Marcelo Porto of Concordia brokerage. \par \par \uc2  Sao Paulo's blue chip Bovespa index closed 1.47 percent stronger at 11,700 points, bringing the market's gains this month to 5.4 percent. It is up 2 percent so far this week. Volume was a moderate 467 million reais ($233 million). \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones industrial average rose over 2.2 percent, finishing at 10,622 points. \par \par \uc2  "The market had every reason to perform well today with U.S. shares rising and good local news," said Padua. \par \par \uc2  "Brazil made clear it could sell additional reserves to calm down the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at least until December. Money from the newly-launched bonds will also boost reserves. Turbulence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has been a big concern recently." \par \par \uc2  Added Concordia's Porto: "The day was very active. Sellers didn't have a chance. If it weren't for technical problems at the bourse, which sidelined foreigners a bit, we could have registered a bigger rise." \par \par \uc2  The bourse's data feed failed to update for a couple of hours in the morning. \par \par \uc2  Phone operator Embratel rose 3 percent on growing optimism that the government was likely to negotiate the company's back taxes. \par \par \uc2  Among other blue chips, benchmark stock Telebras rose 2.78 percent to 151.8 reais. Petrobras preferred edged up 0.06 percent to 314.10 reais. Eletrobras preferred shares were among the few day's losers, slipping 0.31 percent to 35.41 reais. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Arminio Fraga said Thursday Brazil planned to cut the floor for the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $2 billion, which would give \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  more flexibility to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The market also warmed to Brazil's successful sovereign bond issue of 500 million euros. The government had initially placed 300 million euros, but increased the size in just a few hours on the back of good market reception. \par \par \uc2  The real has firmed for two days in a row and now stands at 1.974 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvas011i5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
