\par\par \b \uc2  IMF says talked to Brazil on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  reserves. \b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1999\par 18:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON, Oct 28 (Reuters) - The International Monetary Fund said on Thursday it has had talks with Brazil on the level of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves there. \par \par \uc2  "Informal discussions have taken place already," IMF external relations chief Thomas Dawson told a news briefing. \par \par \uc2  Dawson said the IMF technical team would only be able to make recommendations and not to make decisions on the issue. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, after the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell through the 2-per-1 dollar level in early trade. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in August, but has more frequently used dollar-indexed domestic debt auctions to take pressure off the real. \par \par \uc2  ((Washington newsroom, +1 202 898-8310, fax +1 202 898-8383, washington.economic.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvas01036\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
